{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage","id":440349,"title":"Brainstorming a Pinocchio Lineage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-13T12:57:01-07:00","id":440349,"title":"Brainstorming a Pinocchio Lineage","content":"Hello everybody.<br /> <br /> After reading some numbers of the little gem that is Fables, aside from the blunt need to run a Changeling game heavily inspired from it, I've also been thinking about an old project of mine kinda related to fairy tales as well: a Promethean Lineage inspired by Pinocchio.<br /> <br /> Aside from the obvious analogies between the original novel and a Pilgrimage, some specific aspects of the story sounds pretty Promethean too: Pinocchio dies and returns to life once, changes his attitude abrutply during his journey (as if he changed a Refinement), ordinary people who meet him either want to exploit, enslave or kill him and there are also a couple of monstrous beasts (and a strange, intelligent ogre) that try to eat the little marionette. My point being, the potential for a Lineage is not hard to see.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm here because I only have a few ideas in mind and could use some discussion.<br /> <br /> I thought about playing a bit with the connection with Pinocchio and the Blue Fairy, making this a Lineage somewhat influenced by the Fae in the same way the Ulgan are related to spirits. This could be done in the first place either by Geppetto using the body of the Changeling that was once his son or a mixture of human corpses and Fetch remains to create the &quot;marionette&quot;, but these are only the first thoughts I had. No idea yet about how this connection with the Fae would influence the Promethean's Pilgrimage after its creation.<br /> <br /> For the Bestowments, I've been thinking about something lie-related or the ability to have a some sort of little companion, perhaps ephemeral, that grants a bonus on Humanity rolls and/or helps the Promethean on the Pilgrimace (making it earn more Vitriol, for example)<br /> <br /> Disquiet and Wasteland are a bit harder. Generally speaking, in the novel people were always trying to enslave Pinocchio and use him to satisfy their desires, even if Pinocchio himself had nothing to do with it in the first place, so it's possible to work on that for the Disquiet. As for the Wasteland, I have not the faintest idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, any thoughts or suggestions? Even ones that have nothing to do with what I have in mind are welcomed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-13-2015, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:03:45-07:00","id":440451,"title":"","content":"Using the remains of a Fetch makes total sense. Wooden puppet, simulacrum made from sticks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:40:14-07:00","id":440528,"title":"","content":"Hm, Wastelands are all about the Promethean's element becoming corrupted and out of control.<br /> <br /> Maybe something to do with Wood? I get the sense the Lineage is all about &quot;growing up&quot;, so being linked to the element of Wood makes sense. A Puppet's Wasteland causes any wood to grow unruly and disobedient, much like they are during Torment (Pinocchio was a punk in the original story).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:18:29-07:00","id":440652,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting that in the original book, Pinocchio started out as a log that could talk; then Gepetto fashioned it into the wooden marrionette. Using the remains of a Fetch to make a Promethean fits nicely with this notion.<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, the Cricket was an Elpidim, a <i>qashmal</i> who guides Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-18-2015, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:29:04-07:00","id":440742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=440652#post440652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth noting that in e original book, Pinocchio started out as a log that could talk; then Gepetto fashioned it into the wooden marrionette. Using the remains of a Fetch to make a Promeean fits nicely with this notion.<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, the Cricket was an Elpidim, a <i>qashmal</i> who guides Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite, although I think the singular is Elpidos.<br /> <br /> Also, I think Pinocchio <i>kills</i> the Cricket in the book. Like after one chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=440528#post440528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, Wastelands are all about the Promethean's element becoming corrupted and out of control.<br /> <br /> Maybe something to do with Wood? I get the sense the Lineage is all about &quot;growing up&quot;, so being linked to the element of Wood makes sense. A Puppet's Wasteland causes any wood to grow unruly and disobedient, much like they are during Torment (Pinocchio was a punk in the original story).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just wood, but all non-animal life. Plants, fungi, bacteria, etc. Would be pretty damn nasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:56:29-07:00","id":440765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=440528#post440528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, Wastelands are all about the Promethean's element becoming corrupted and out of control.<br /> <br /> Maybe something to do with Wood? I get the sense the Lineage is all about &quot;growing up&quot;, so being linked to the element of Wood makes sense. A Puppet's Wasteland causes any wood to grow unruly and disobedient, much like they are during Torment (Pinocchio was a punk in the original story).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice idea. That reminds me that I completely forgot about Torment. For it to make the Promethean rebellious and disobedient fits perfectly. You also pointed out a great theme for the Lineage, and that's going to help a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=440742#post440742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite, although I think the singular is Elpidos.<br /> <br /> Also, I think Pinocchio <i>kills</i> the Cricket in the book. Like after one chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>With a mallet, if I'm not mistaken. It's been a while. It later returns as a ghost, but yeah. It probably works better as a <i>qashmal </i>than as a Bestowment familiar though, so I'd say you make a good point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=440742#post440742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just wood, but all non-animal life. Plants, fungi, bacteria, etc. Would be pretty damn nasty.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would be quite horrible indeed. The kind of mayhem that fits a Wasteland. I'm not sure about bacteria, but flora and fungi sound great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-13-2015, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T19:02:10-07:00","id":440769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=440765#post440765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be quite horrible indeed. The kind of mayhem that fits a Wasteland. I'm not sure about bacteria, but flora and fungi sound great.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What do you mean, 'the superstructure's more black mold than wood'? The building was constructed <i>last year</i>!&quot; <i>pause</i> &quot;<b><i>WHAT?!</i></b> How in the name of <i>sweet baby <b>FUCK</b></i> do tree roots penetrate brand-new <i>steel </i>pipes?!&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, imagine the E. coli in your gut (AKA &quot;intestinal flora&quot;, which is reason enough in my book to lump 'em in) breeding out of control, until you've got what basically amounts to &quot;shit, minus the partially-digested food&quot; overflowing from both ends.<br /> <br /> You're welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-13-2015, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T23:57:02-07:00","id":441035,"title":"","content":"...if you guys are making Pinocchio out of the remains of a Fetch and aspecting him to Wood, you may as well go all the way and base the Wasteland off the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T00:00:47-07:00","id":441036,"title":"","content":"Considering that puppet is basically synonomous with bad liar, I wouldn't give them a liar power, I'd make that part of their disquiet- People find them untrustworthy, don't believe them (especially when they lie), etc<br /> <br /> As for the wasteland effect, I'd go with something a bit more fae- Morality Play: As the wasteland sets in, the laws of probability warp, punishing misdeeds. As the wasteland gets worse, more minor misdeeds get punished, or the punishments get harsher and harsher. A bonafide saint might be safe, that is, if something happening to them isn't part of someone elses punishment, and of course, pure goodness (laughably rare in the nwod to begin with) would certainly get harder after disaster after disaster.<br /> <br /> As for their bestowment, I'd go with &quot;Not a real boy yet:&quot; Being made out of wood, the promethean can not only heal as normal, but be repaired, replacing limbs with relative ease (access to wood, an extended roll on crafts). The promethean can even be resurrected from the dead, with a helper getting enough successes on a craft roll, and a loss of permanent azoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 03-14-2015, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T01:25:56-07:00","id":441076,"title":"","content":"In terms of disquiet, I could actually see that, much like Tammuz, people want to exploit the Pinocchio promethean, or take advantage of his gullibility--much like how people try to exploit the character in both the original fairytale and the multiple movie adaptations.<br /> <br /> In fact, I could see this lineage possessing the Sanguine humor, in association with Pinocchio's sociability in the fairytale. <br /> <br /> Their creation right could reflect a tragic story, of how Geppetto lost his mind after losing his son (or finding out his son had been replaced by a fetch), and in a fit of mad grief gathered up all the wooden parts and tried to give it life by putting a child's heart into the lifeless husk. In fact, that's how I would picture the creation right to go--a bunch of wooden parts must be carved and put together in the shape of a child or young person, and it is given life upon the insertion of a heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:24:58-07:00","id":441946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=441035#post441035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...if you guys are making Pinocchio out of the remains of a Fetch and aspecting him to Wood, you may as well go all the way and base the Wasteland off the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=441036#post441036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the wasteland effect, I'd go with something a bit more fae- Morality Play: As the wasteland sets in, the laws of probability warp, punishing misdeeds. As the wasteland gets worse, more minor misdeeds get punished, or the punishments get harsher and harsher. A bonafide saint might be safe, that is, if something happening to them isn't part of someone elses punishment, and of course, pure goodness (laughably rare in the nwod to begin with) would certainly get harder after disaster after disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fantastic ideas. I really like the idea of plant and fungus growth going out of control as the Wasteland begins to develop, until you've basically got something similar to the Hedge. Then, some<i> things</i> resembling the Gentry show up and start abducting people who misbehave (for whatever value of &quot;misbehave&quot; the Storyteller deems fit) and <i>doing</i> shit to them, like, oh, say... turning them into donkeys, maybe ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=441076#post441076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of disquiet, I could actually see that, much like Tammuz, people want to exploit the Pinocchio promethean, or take advantage of his gullibility--much like how people try to exploit the character in both the original fairytale and the multiple movie adaptations.</div> </div> </div> </div>This also fits in with the Fae connection. Maybe make it specifically that people affected by Disquiet develop a Fae-like attitude towards the Pinocchio, wanting to possess him/her as a plaything? After all, on some level you can sense that he/she's just a puppet, a mere toy. It's not like you're taking advantage of a <i>real</i> person ...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T00:36:44-07:00","id":442268,"title":"","content":"Hmm, not what I was going for, but that seems very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T01:47:21-07:00","id":442340,"title":"","content":"Idly, I note that Matt's comments on 2E Unfleshed mention a) that they generally cover human-like representations of all types and b) that their Torment could manifest as submission or rebellion. (It'd be nice to know more, 'cause they could turn out to be a good fit for Pinocchio, but...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T06:42:03-07:00","id":442468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=441036#post441036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that puppet is basically synonomous with bad liar, I wouldn't give them a liar power, I'd make that part of their disquiet- People find them untrustworthy, don't believe them (especially when they lie), etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=441036#post441036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for their bestowment, I'd go with &quot;Not a real boy yet:&quot; Being made out of wood, the promethean can not only heal as normal, but be repaired, replacing limbs with relative ease (access to wood, an extended roll on crafts). The promethean can even be resurrected from the dead, with a helper getting enough successes on a craft roll, and a loss of permanent azoth.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a good one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=441076#post441076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their creation right could reflect a tragic story, of how Geppetto lost his mind after losing his son (or finding out his son had been replaced by a fetch), and in a fit of mad grief gathered up all the wooden parts and tried to give it life by putting a child's heart into the lifeless husk. In fact, that's how I would picture the creation right to go--a bunch of wooden parts must be carved and put together in the shape of a child or young person, and it is given life upon the insertion of a heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I had in mind. Geppetto was a somewhat sad figure even in the original novel and many adaptations already depict it as some sort of tragic lonely man (one with Bob Hoskin's actually adds a lost wife and son to his background, with Pinocchio being his desperate attempt to fill the void) and translating him as a Demiurge in the Wolrd of Darkness only strenghtens this assumptions. The creation process you picture works well: I'd suggest both carving a body and having to insert a human heart and the remains of a Fetch. It makes the process both easier (a heart is a bit less complicated to find than a whole body) and harder, because of the Fetch parts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=441946#post441946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fantastic ideas. I really like the idea of plant and fungus growth going out of control as the Wasteland begins to develop, until you've basically got something similar to the Hedge. Then, some<i> things</i> resembling the Gentry show up and start abducting people who misbehave (for whatever value of &quot;misbehave&quot; the Storyteller deems fit) and <i>doing</i> shit to them, like, oh, say... turning them into donkeys, maybe ...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more or less what I thought. At first, plants get out of control, but at higher levels of the Wasteland strange things begin to happen, the trees bear odd fruits, there are thorns everywhere until when, at the last stage, the whole area is something like a Hedge, with something wandering across these unnatural woodlands and punishing those who dare to break the byzantine laws of the place. Where Ulgan's Wasteland brings forth the Shadow, this brings the Hedge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=441946#post441946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This also fits in with the Fae connection. Maybe make it specifically that people affected by Disquiet develop a Fae-like attitude towards the Pinocchio, wanting to possess him/her as a plaything? After all, on some level you can sense that he/she's just a puppet, a mere toy. It's not like you're taking advantage of a <i>real</i> person ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Frankly, there are so many examples of this in Pinocchio's story that the Disquiet almost writes itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=442340#post442340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idly, I note that Matt's comments on 2E Unfleshed mention a) that they generally cover human-like representations of all types and b) that their Torment could manifest as submission or rebellion. (It'd be nice to know more, 'cause they could turn out to be a good fit for Pinocchio, but...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that would be a nice excuse to give us some new teasers... <i>*winks at developers</i><br /> <br /> I suppose we'll see. At worst, that would mean that this thread only turns out to be a nice discussion about Pinocchio and Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-15-2015, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:56:50-07:00","id":442711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=441946#post441946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This also fits in with the Fae connection. Maybe make it specifically that people affected by Disquiet develop a Fae-like attitude towards the Pinocchio, wanting to possess him/her as a plaything? After all, on some level you can sense that he/she's just a puppet, a mere toy. It's not like you're taking advantage of a <i>real</i> person ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just the Promethian; but anyone too weak to protest.<br /> <br /> This is the True Fae. Their touch should be nasty.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:03:18-07:00","id":442825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=442711#post442711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just the Promethian; but anyone too weak to protest.<br /> <br /> This is the True Fae. Their touch should be nasty.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Damn</i>.<br /> <br /> So a Pinocchio's Disquiet turns everyone around them into a toxic narcissist?<br /> <br /> As someone who's in love with a mild narcissist*, I have to say that the thought of EVERYONE adopting a malignantly self<i>ish</i> (&quot;I am aware of your needs, I just don't give a shit&quot;) rather than the merely immaturely self-<i>centered</i> (&quot;I'm too wrapped up in my own issues to consider that you might have problems too&quot;) narcissism I'm all too familiar with gives me the legit heebie-jeebies.<br /> <br /> *In case anyone cares to read about my personal life, she's an emotionally damaged serial monogamist/commitment-phobe whose record with a guy is 3 months and averages less than 1; there's an inverse relationship between long-term potential and how long she actually sticks around because, to her, commitment = a trap that robs you of your freedom and eats your soul, because that's what happened to her dad. She's managed to keep me as a fixed point in her life for more than 6 years only by denying and repressing the obvious attraction for me that everyone around us can see.<br /> <br /> Yes, I'm aware that she needs therapy. I'm not even going to <i>think</i> about dating her unless I can get her back in my therapist's office (I already got her to come in for 3 sessions) on an ongoing basis. And yes, there <i>are</i> other prospects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:11:15-07:00","id":442833,"title":"","content":"Maybe we should also allow this Lineage a specialized set of contract-like transmutations that they can choose from? Sort of like the Zeka and their radioactive Transmutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:39:55-07:00","id":442973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=442825#post442825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Pinocchio's Disquiet turns everyone around them into a toxic narcissist?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more of a kidnapping slaver; but without the whole &quot;take them to another country to avoid the law&quot; because Disquiet effects everyone and thus slavery becomes normalized.<br /> <br /> Basically I'm going by Disney's Pinocchio because that's the only version I've seen and the True Fae who're very... unsubtle about the fact you're their slave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T13:36:49-07:00","id":443051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=442973#post442973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking more of a kidnapping slaver; but without the whole &quot;take them to another country to avoid the law&quot; because Disquiet effects everyone and thus slavery becomes normalized.<br /> <br /> Basically I'm going by Disney's Pinocchio because that's the only version I've seen and the True Fae who're very... unsubtle about the fact you're their slave.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has... Certain disturbing implications regarding the effects on the supernatural landscape. What would happen to the Shadow in a region affected by high levels of Pinocchian Disquiet? And a prevailing might-makes-right philosophy where people are taking slaves left and right, with the resulting desperation from the enslaved... Hmm. I'll have to open my copy of Inferno when I get home, but it seems like &quot;spirits of oppression&quot; plus &quot;tormented souls&quot; plus &quot;the downtrodden wanting power to overthrow their masters&quot; is a fine recipe for creating/attracting a couple different types of demon.<br /> <br /> And that's BEFORE adding in the fact that the Pinocchio is likely to be one of the slaves, which means you're probably going to have a Wasteland develop on top of all this.<br /> <br /> So then the Hedge-alike develops and the twisted faux-Fae (can we call them Bogeymen? Is that name taken already?) emerge to punish &quot;wrongdoers,&quot; which there'll be no shortage of at this point.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the stories developing from all this are so riveting that the True Fae start to take notice...<br /> <br /> The story almost writes itself, doesn't it? The Gentry start grabbing people and leave Fetches in their place, which gives the Pinocchio plenty of raw material for attempting to create another of his kind. All he needs is a fresh human heart. PER ATTEMPT.<br /> <br /> Honestly, a Pinocchio Lineage would make a GREAT source of antagonists under this model. After their Progenitor's experiences, they figured out that they could roll into a remote town, let their Disquiet turn it into a haven for slavers, then keep their heads down while the Wasteland develops and the Bogeymen slaughter their masters. Then, in the aftermath, they become the saviors of the surviving former slaves, whom they lead to settle in another town. But their Disquiet is still in full effect, so the whole thing starts over.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, they get plenty of corpses to use for parts, and even if the Fae don't show up, there's always the possibility that there's already a Fetch present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-15-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T18:21:16-07:00","id":443463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deceptors are the product of sinful thoughts that manifest on the Astral Plane, the realm of dreams. [...] When people work toward a common, terrible end, the spirits of collective dreams and aspirations carry that darkness. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Immundi are the impure Shadow-spirits that symbolize the tie between moral and spiritual corruption. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Larvals are the Twilight echoes of unrepentant, evil individuals. </div> </div> </div>I can see the proposed Disquiet effects of the Pinocchio Lineage resulting in all three types of Diaboli if it really goes unchecked for a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T01:45:19-07:00","id":443916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=442973#post442973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically I'm going by Disney's Pinocchio because that's the only version I've seen</div> </div> </div> </div>FYI, the original is in public domain: <a href=\"http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Adventures_of_Pinocchio\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Ad...s_of_Pinocchio</a> I have not read it either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T01:47:31-07:00","id":443917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=443051#post443051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So then the Hedge-alike develops and the twisted faux-Fae (can we call them Bogeymen? Is that name taken already?) emerge to punish &quot;wrongdoers,&quot; which there'll be no shortage of at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say actual Fae; the Blue Faery has to have an angle. I'd say she's also part of the generative act, if a Pinocchio wants to create another Pinocchio she's contractually obliged to do her part, and tends to be pretty happy if someone else asks her to help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=443051#post443051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, a Pinocchio Lineage would make a GREAT source of antagonists under this model.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see them as antagonists. More like<br /> <br /> Mr. Varney &quot;I'm not saying you should kill them, I'm just saying I wouldn't blame you if you did.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said; the Pilgramage doesn't say you have to create another Promethian of your own Lineage. If you see a Pinocchio trying to create more of it's kind...<br /> <br /> <br /> Also don't forget that the True Fae's slavery is a metaphor for abuse. Don't let slavery themed plots distract from the more straight forward abuse plots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:59:25-07:00","id":443965,"title":"","content":"Well you could make the boogeymen a type of hobgoblin that is particularly attracted to pinnochio wastelands, and while they're there snatch people up to sell them as slaves or food in goblin markets or to true fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T04:56:34-07:00","id":444044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=443965#post443965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well you could make the boogeymen a type of hobgoblin that is particularly attracted to pinnochio wastelands, and while they're there snatch people up to sell them as slaves or food in goblin markets or to true fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not as familiar with Changeling as some of the other lines. Are Hobgoblins bound by the same complicated oaths and contracts and codes of behavior.as Changelings and True Fae? If so, they could easily be bound.to enforce a twisted.form of &quot;eye for an eye&quot; justice and only kidnap slavers, while leaving the slaves alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T08:30:42-07:00","id":444304,"title":"","content":"No more than changelings by default, but since one would be creating a new race one could certainly give them a racial geas.<br /> <br /> Perhaps they are the blue faerie's servants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:04:51-07:00","id":444459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=444044#post444044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not as familiar with Changeling as some of the other lines. Are Hobgoblins bound by the same complicated oaths and contracts and codes of behavior.as Changelings and True Fae? If so, they could easily be bound.to enforce a twisted.form of &quot;eye for an eye&quot; justice and only kidnap slavers, while leaving the slaves alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why would we want to make them less evil and horrific?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:16:30-07:00","id":444591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=444459#post444459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But why would we want to make them less evil and horrific?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just spitballing possibilities here. I'm thinking the Bogeymen enforce a twisted, heavily ironic form of <i>lex talionis</i>. Doing unto you as you have done unto others.<br /> <br /> And hey, maybe they don't leave the slaves alone so much as just not abducting them. But, <i>you</i> are guilty of such-and-such a crime, here's <i>your</i> punishment. And <i>you</i> did this other thing, so here's <i>your</i> retribution. And they're very expansive in what they consider an infraction.<br /> <br /> Think of the kind of shit ISIS considers &quot;justice.&quot; Or the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jWshPH_jsjQ\" target=\"_blank\">boardroom scene from Dogma</a>, if Loki and Bartleby were more creative than to assign &quot;death&quot; as the penalty for literally every offense.<br /> <br /> There doesn't even have to be what we'd consider consistency to the system. They can punish people for keeping slaves <i>and</i> punish slaves for not obeying their masters; whereas we'd consider that to be illogical, they'd see it as completely in keeping with their nature.<br /> <br /> This could <i>add</i> to the horror \u2014 the Bogeymen roll in and abduct the slavers, leaving the former slaves thinking that they're in the clear. Then, the Bogeymen come <i>back</i> and establish kangaroo courts a la The Dark Knight Rises. Or maybe they just begin meting out punishment and don't bother with the formality, although I rather like the image of basically <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i-dJPoSlPfU\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> but with the Blue Faery presiding and Bogeymen as court officers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:24:15-07:00","id":444979,"title":"","content":"PS: Evil Pinocchio + Disquietism = lulz.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:01:30-07:00","id":445036,"title":"","content":"Keep it simple. The Bogeymen are not the focus of an entire story. They're a background event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:05:26-07:00","id":445039,"title":"","content":"Marionette Wastelands<br /> <br /> The Pinocchio Prometheans belong to the element of wood, and their connection to the Hedge is undeniable. When they linger in an area, it takes on the attributes of that realm, first superficially and then metaphysically, before finally opening Trods through which Bogeymen emerge.<br /> <br /> Stage Two \u2014 Plants and fungi grow at an impossible rate. Weeds choke the lawns, tree roots rupture sidewalks from beneath, and black mold renders brand-new homes uninhabitable.<br /> <br /> Stage Three \u2014 Children are plagued by nightmares of Bogeymen in their closets and under their beds. Buildings collapse, their walls torn apart and <i>replaced</i> by fungi and trees in a bizarre sort of fossilization; residents without any other recourse may just shrug their shoulders and move back in.<br /> <br /> Stage Four \u2014 Trods appear everywhere and the Bogeymen (Hobgoblins contracted to the Blue Faery) show up to enforce the most horrific form of ironic, Bronze Age-esque pseudo-justice imaginable; nearly everyone is &quot;guilty&quot; of some offense for which the punishment is both extreme and horrific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T17:34:05-07:00","id":445102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=445036#post445036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep it simple. The Bogeymen are not the focus of an entire story. They're a background event.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they don't actually show up unless a Pinocchio's Wasteland hits Stage Four, so they only become a major part of a story if the Storyteller or the Pinocchio's player really wants them to. And of course, in the latter case, it's subject to ST approval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T00:52:16-07:00","id":445435,"title":"","content":"Which is why you keep it simple. By stage 4 of the wasteland you're already in the endgame or leaving that location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T05:08:05-07:00","id":445597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=445435#post445435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why you keep it simple. By stage 4 of the wasteland you're already in the endgame or leaving that location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it's a plot hook caused by an NPC Pinocchio. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T23:38:53-07:00","id":509651,"title":"","content":"All of this has been phenomenal to read. I will absolutely be borrowing this for a future game. Really cool read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5985-jessel","name":"Jessel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T10:58:16-07:00","id":527889,"title":"","content":"I could see combining some of these ideas with this: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/116LMdtMWBsdZwyaCHquaPa0_qVjmVtQFBMDEGgyo9NQ/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...9NQ/edit?pli=1</a><br /> Perhaps Vittoria escaped from her Keeper, went crazy(er), and is now the Blue Faery?<br /> <br /> It occurred to me some time ago that the preferred substance for making Unfleshed Riven is birch wood, and their Generative act involves sending a body into the Shadow, to be torn apart and reassembled by the beings there...<br /> <br /> Also, what about some kind of Fetch/Pandoran Mockery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 05-29-2015, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T08:24:16-07:00","id":538389,"title":"","content":"I actually really like this idea. None of those links worked for me, but did this end up going anywhere? Any preliminary write up attempts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4024-storysanctum","name":"storysanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T09:08:30-07:00","id":538468,"title":"","content":"It's in the &quot;things I have to do after I'm done with my exams&quot; corner of my mind, along with tons of other stuff. I opened the topic to make ideas fly around and I found it an extremely helpful and interesting conversation.<br /> <br /> A couple of months and I should be able to post more easily (as in, posting in the first place) and, after doing a couple of things and reviews of other fanmade works I promised to do ages ago, I'll get to this. I don't forget all these ideas and commitments: it's the time that's lacking.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:12:38-07:00","id":540032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>storysanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/440349-brainstorming-a-pinocchio-lineage?p=538389#post538389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually really like this idea. None of those links worked for me, but did this end up going anywhere? Any preliminary write up attempts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Try this one:<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/116LMdtMWBsdZwyaCHquaPa0_qVjmVtQFBMDEGgyo9NQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Or just go to this thread:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/504812-how-could-a-demon-be-a-demiurge\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/504812-how-could-a-demon-be-a-demiurge\"> How could a Demon be a demiurge - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/504812-how-could-a-demon-be-a-demiurge\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/504812-how-could-a-demon-be-a-demiurge </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I've been reading Saturnine nights and it explains how you need to abandon the supernatural to draw on the Divine Flame, to create a promethean. It seems unlikely that one of the unchained could do that.....but the book proves that the impossible isn't always impossible. What would it take? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 06-04-2015, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T20:48:12-07:00","id":563693,"title":"","content":"My thoughts, as a Changeling addict: <br /> <br /> Hedge Gates should open starting earlier in the Wasteland. They're dangerous by default, but not *inherently* NopeBadWrong - until the Pinocchio's Wasteland draws the Hobgoblins/Huntsmen/True Fae in. <br /> <br /> Part of the Wasteland should include a preponderance of thorned and stinging plants, to suit the Hedge's thematics. Bushes grow into briars, gardens overgrow with thistles. Making the area inherently twisty and easy to get lost in would also suit the thematics, especially combined with the hedge gates. <br /> <br /> I can see (off the top of my head) a couple potential Bestowment ideas. The &quot;repair&quot; Bestowment (similar to the Frankensteinian &quot;Spare Parts&quot;?) is an option. I think the other should be an ability to either swear a supernatural Oath (gaining power from it) or bind others to a supernatural Pledge (inflicting horrible punishment if broken). Oaths and pledges are just too central to the Changeling mythos to ignore when crossing over. <br /> <br /> Do you want these Pinocchios to be more like the Lost, more like Fetches, or like some unholy conglomeration of the two, with thematics torn from each?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T00:50:47-07:00","id":563798,"title":"","content":"I already suggested a bestowment like spare parts, a power based on oaths doesn't really fit thematically with a lineage that started with someone not only synonymous with liar, but bad liar.<br /> <br /> As for your question, why make them like anything? Prometheans are only reflective of their creators in so much as they are reflections of the creation ritual used. Of the supernatural made lineages as examples, you have a rather vampire like promethean whose humour is vitae (so naturally, what else would he be like?), a lineage of lunatics whose humour is moonlight, and a mage made lineage that is occult but not really mage like at all. <br /> <br /> So any similarities to changelings, fetches, or true fae should come organically from what the pinocchios are, not something shoehorned in. <br /> <br /> For example, the original story is about a puppet made from magical wood. A natural thing to do would be to make that original piece of wood from the hedge. So a connection to the hedge is as natural thing to throw in, but the only creatures native to the hedge are hobgoblins, and they are such a diverse lot they're is no point in trying to make them like hobgoblins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T19:49:42-07:00","id":564878,"title":"","content":"I was actually referring to your posted suggestion when I mentioned the self-repair Bestowment, StSword. As for Pinocchio's poor lying skills, that just means that members of his Lineage will have to be more deceptive and manipulative with the truth, if they maintain that sort of weakness. The Fae from the Dresden Files series are a good example of how well that sort of thing can work.<br /> <br /> For why I think an oathbinding bestowment would be appropriate: The Hedge is a place of Wyrd, of Glamour and Fae magic, and all of Fae magic is based on oaths and agreements - literally, the Fae exist and can affect the world only because they mutually agree to exist and have made deals with reality to allow it to affect them. All the various Fae powers are based on eldritch pacts with reality. I feel like a Promethean with ties to Glamour, the Hedge, or Fae reality would have to include some form of oaths (if only thematically), because oaths are part and parcel of the Fae.<br /> <br /> I could see thematic ties to both Changelings and Fetches. Fetches, especially, are also simulacra which appear human, and drawing parallels between the two could help highlight the similarities and differences between the two kinds of creatures. Direct Changeling thematic ties are a bit less obvious, but they definitely exist - Changelings are people with an inhuman body and a soul that's a patchwork of Glamour. Prometheans are people with an inhuman (proto)soul and a body that's a patchwork of human parts and Pyros. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}